# hope-metrics-platform — agent constraints

## Git

- Never create commits (`git commit`).
- Never push (`git push`), including upstream or force push.
- Never amend, rebase, or tag for the user.
- Do not `git add` unless the user explicitly asks for add commands or staging.
- The user commits and pushes manually.

## Language and content

- No Chinese in docs, comments, commit message suggestions, or user-facing repo text. English only.
- No secrets in the repo: passwords, credentialed `DATABASE_URL`, absolute machine paths, private planning notes.
- Prefer bland, direct engineering prose. Avoid hype, slogan-y openers, emoji, and filler ("robust", "seamless", "powerful", "production-grade", "aims to", tutorial padding) unless the user asks for marketing copy.

## Architecture

- Ingest owns `raw_*` writes. dbt owns stg/mart transforms. Do not reintroduce `warehouse/*.sql` as the publish path.
- Probe (this repo) and simulator (separate repo) share the device event contract; do not merge simulator into this repo.
- Work step by step. Before coding a step: state the motivation and wait for explicit agreement. Do not implement later MVP pieces (Airflow, Metabase, etc.) without agreement.
